  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc100-200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 202.20 Participants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 202.20 “Participants” means:\n\n(a) For an adjudicative proceeding, all respondent(s), respondent’s representative(s), intervenor(s), intervenor’s representative(s), and prosecutor(s) for that adjudicative proceeding; or\n\n(b) For a non-adjudicative proceeding, the collective group of individuals who attend or otherwise participate in the public hearing held on the matter or provide comments orally or in writing on paper or by e-mail, or any combination thereof.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Plc 200) #13427, eff 8-4-22; ss by #13837, eff 12-28-23 (formerly Plc 202.17) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Plc 200); ss by #14136, eff 12-1-24 (formerly Plc 202.27)",
